in @facet
in @facet/metalogue
in @facet/metalogue/materialize
in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @nl

# @facet/gestalt — the .gestalt altitude grammar.
#
# `.gestalt` files are the file-level projection of a @gestalt graph
# per Alex 2026-08-03 verbatim ratification:
#
#   *"@facet/gestalt makes sense. .gestalt files becomes the file level
#    projection of the graph."*
#
# Sibling to @facet/mirror (shards/code/mirror.mirror; the mirror-
# altitude grammar), @facet/rust (shards/code/rust.mirror), @facet/gleam
# (shards/code/gleam.mirror), @facet/llvm, @facet/turing under the
# universal @facet discipline (shards/code.mirror). Each declares the
# five operations on its own source manifold; @facet/gestalt names
# `.gestalt` as ONE such altitude — the `@gestalt`-family's
# graph-as-file surface.
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# The .gestalt corpus already exists at
# `/Users/reed/dev/systemic.engineering/blog/pieces/3published/` (19
# pieces published 2026-03-08 to present per Taut scout 2026-08-03).
# The register was crystallized by Alex Wolf in-authorship long before
# this grammar-decl mint. This shard does NOT invent a format — it
# NAMES the format that already exists. Per
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]].
#
# Corpus grep-witnessed patterns extracted from the 19-piece register
# (see §The .gestalt register below for enumerated productions):
#
#   frontmatter        `---\n<yaml>\n---`             (Piece-Consciousness :2)
#   heading-hierarchy  `# / ## / ###`                  (Piece-Fragmentation)
#   asymmetric-close   `..\n` breath-mark              (universal)
#   inline-annotation  `[[Actor]]`                     (Piece-Distributed :56)
#   inline-annotation  `[[Fragmentation|link-text]]`   (Piece-Distributed :103)
#   corpus-link        `[text](wiki:Piece - X)`        (Piece-Consciousness :86)
#   external-link      `[text](https://…)`             (universal)
#   parenthetical-aside `(...)` and `(...]`            (Piece-Agents :1, :16)
#   asymmetric-brackets `(...]` intentional            (Piece-Agents `..\n(And the absurd idea of a singularity.]`)
#   code-span          `` `END LOOP` ``                (Piece-Agents :24, :30)
#   density-marker     `TL;DR: <string>`               (universal at section-ends)
#   emphasis           `**bold**` / `*emphasis*`       (Piece-Consciousness sources)
#   emoji-first-class  `🌱 🌈 📉` inline               (universal signature)
#   citation-inline    `— [Name](URL)`                 (Piece-Consciousness :43)
#   quote-block        `> …` multi-line                (universal)
#   line-break-as-structure  each newline = semantic  (universal architectural)
#   soft-break-marker  `\\\n` (line-continuation)       (Piece-Fragmentation §1 opener)
#   section-cluster    `## When Agents X` pattern     (Piece-Agents)
#   separator          `---` between sections          (Piece-Consciousness)
#   table              `| col | col |\n|---|---|`      (Piece-Consciousness sources)
#   list-item          `- item` and `1. item`          (universal)
#
# The register IS load-bearing, not decoration. The grammar preserves
# WHAT ALEX WROTE, not what a sanitized markdown parser would accept.
# Per Reed 2026-08-03 mint-charter register-honoring discipline.
#
# === why sibling to @facet/mirror (not sub-species of @gestalt) ===
#
# Two arguments per the @facet/mirror precedent (shards/code/mirror.mirror):
#
#   1. Path-namespace property (load-bearing per
#      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]): this file at
#      `shards/code/gestalt.mirror` declares `@facet/gestalt`. Same
#      shape as `shards/code/mirror.mirror` declares `@facet/mirror`.
#      The path IS the declaration.
#
#   2. Sibling discipline: @facet/gestalt joins @facet/rust, @facet/gleam,
#      @facet/mirror, @facet/llvm, @facet/turing as instances of the
#      universal @facet discipline. Reading the family flat-namespaced
#      makes the substrate-pull recognition legible ("`.gestalt` is
#      one of the altitudes @facet knows about").
#
# @gestalt (family-root at shards/gestalt.mirror) carries the
# document-as-song-unfolding semantics (nodes/edges/annotations/
# unfolding_state). @facet/gestalt names WHAT A .gestalt FILE IS at
# the grammar altitude — the file-level projection of that graph.
# Different altitudes; both required; no collapse.
#
# === the file-level projection of the graph (Alex 2026-08-03) ===
#
# Per Alex verbatim: `.gestalt files becomes the file level projection
# of the graph`. The gestalt_document carrier at shards/gestalt.mirror
# is:
#
#   type gestalt_document = {
#     root, source_position, author, visibility_scope,
#     song_ref, nodes, edges, modes, annotations,
#   }
#
# The `.gestalt` file grammar projects this graph structure to a
# linear byte surface. The projection is bijective under the round-trip
# law (see @facet/mirror.round_trip precedent): for every valid
# gestalt_document, `parse(render(doc)) = doc` structurally. The file
# carries what the graph carries; nothing more, nothing less.
#
# Two composition legs consume this grammar:
#
#   - `@cascade/code/mirror/gestalt` (mint queue) — the first leg of
#     the composition theorem chain (mirror substrate → gestalt IR).
#     Source grammar = @facet/mirror; target grammar = @facet/gestalt.
#   - `@cascade/code/gestalt/gleam` (mint queue) — the second leg
#     (gestalt IR → gleam via gestalt-ui library). Source grammar =
#     @facet/gestalt; target grammar = @facet/gleam. Emits gestalt-ui-
#     shaped Gleam per Alex Q-C2 adjudication (not arbitrary Gleam).
#
# === five operations at the .gestalt altitude ===
#
# Per the prism-as-trait-as-everything discipline (per
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]), declaring
# @facet/gestalt IS declaring the five operations on the .gestalt-source
# manifold. The operation signatures inherit from @facet; the altitude
# specialization names what each verb does at THIS altitude. Bodies
# are `\` per consumer-pull discipline — the FLOOR resolver (Reed Tick
# under [substrate-floor:@io-boundary]) discharges them once the
# cascade legs land.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/2026-08-03-mara-distributed-colony-canonical-
#               spec.md §The .gestalt register (this shard's canonical
#               spec companion; §.gestalt grammar spec extracted from
#               19-piece corpus grep-hits, NOT invented).
#               docs/math/2026-08-03-mara-distributed-colony-5d-quantum-
#               foam-formalization.md §Composition theorem (§mirror →
#               gestalt → gleam → js cascade chain).
#               docs/scouts/2026-08-03-taut-distributed-colony-substrate-
#               scout.md §1.6 (target-agnostic gestalt-ui shape).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (the
#                      lift is Alex's 2026-08-03 verbatim ratification
#                      + the 19-piece corpus that already exists;
#                      NOT re-derived),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the corpus already crystallized the register;
#                      this shard NAMES the format, does not invent it),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (every action
#                      body `\` blocked; FLOOR realization domain).
# Related shards: shards/code.mirror (universal parent),
#                 shards/code/mirror.mirror (sibling precedent shape),
#                 shards/code/gleam.mirror (target grammar for second
#                                           cascade leg),
#                 shards/gestalt.mirror (family-root carrying graph
#                                        semantics this grammar projects),
#                 shards/cascade/code/mirror/gestalt.mirror (mint queue;
#                                                            first
#                                                            composition
#                                                            leg),
#                 shards/cascade/code/gestalt/gleam.mirror (mint queue;
#                                                           second
#                                                           composition
#                                                           leg).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/code/gestalt.mirror`
# declares `@facet/gestalt` and only that.

# === The .gestalt register — grammar declaration ===
#
# Extracted from grep-witnessed 19-piece corpus at
# `/Users/reed/dev/systemic.engineering/blog/pieces/3published/*.gestalt`
# (2026-03-08 through present; Alex Wolf authorship). NOT invented; the
# grammar names what already exists on disk.
#
# Per @facet/mirror/grammar precedent (shards/code/mirror.mirror lines
# 149-183): whitespace by substrate convention admits space, tab,
# carriage return, AND newline. Under `.gestalt` register discipline,
# newline is LOAD-BEARING (each newline = semantic break, not markdown-
# flow); the grammar preserves the line-break structure the corpus
# already carries.
#
# Path-namespace note: this grammar block declares
# `@facet/gestalt/grammar` under the path-namespace property
# ([[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]).

grammar @facet/gestalt/grammar("gestalt") {
  in @meta

  # ===== lexical primitives =====
  # `line` = the semantic unit at .gestalt altitude. Per corpus
  # discipline, each line carries independent meaning; newlines
  # are NOT flow-joins (as in prose markdown) but structure-marks.
  fixed whitespace_no_newline  = repeat(charset(space_tab), 0, none)
  fixed newline                = literal("\n")
  fixed line                   = repeat(charset(non_newline), 0, none)
  fixed identifier             = repeat(charset(word_char), 1, none)

  # ===== frontmatter =====
  # YAML metadata between two `---` fences. Corpus witness:
  # Piece-Consciousness :1-6 (Status/Author/SLUG/Excerpt).
  # Piece-Fragmentation, Piece-AI, Piece-Distributed Systems.
  fixed fence                  = literal("---")
  fixed frontmatter_body       = until_fence
  fixed frontmatter            = seq(fence, newline, frontmatter_body, fence, newline)

  # ===== heading hierarchy =====
  # ATX-style with #, ##, ###. Corpus witness: universal.
  # Piece-Agents "## When Agents Enter the Room"; Piece-Fragmentation
  # "## 1. On Tech Debt...".
  fixed heading_marker         = repeat(literal("#"), 1, 6)
  fixed heading                = seq(heading_marker, whitespace_no_newline, line, newline)

  # ===== breath-mark / asymmetric close =====
  # `..\n` on its own line = pause/breath/asymmetric-close of the
  # preceding thought. LOAD-BEARING to Alex's register per
  # Piece-Distributed :36 ("Yeah, yeah, I got it.\n> ..") and
  # Piece-Consciousness :46 ("I think too.\n(Am I?)"). Not markdown
  # ellipsis — a first-class structural pause.
  fixed breath_mark            = seq(literal(".."), newline)

  # ===== parenthetical-aside carriers =====
  # `(text)` for symmetric aside; `(text]` for asymmetric close.
  # Both attested in Piece-Agents :1 "Smith will suffice.]" and
  # :16 "(And the absurd idea of a singularity.]". The asymmetric
  # close is intentional; the grammar accepts BOTH and does not
  # normalize. Per register-honoring discipline (Reed 2026-08-03
  # charter): "do not sanitize."
  fixed paren_aside_symmetric  = seq(literal("("), until_close_paren, literal(")"))
  fixed paren_aside_asymmetric = seq(literal("("), until_close_bracket, literal("]"))
  fixed paren_aside            = variant(paren_aside_symmetric, paren_aside_asymmetric)

  # ===== inline annotation `[[X]]` =====
  # First-class annotation carrier. Composes with
  # @gestalt.annotation address at graph altitude. Two shapes:
  # - `[[Actor]]` — bare reference (Piece-Distributed :56).
  # - `[[Fragmentation|display text]]` — reference with display alias
  #   (Piece-Distributed :103 "[[Fragmentation|fragmenting]]").
  fixed annotation_bare        = seq(literal("[["), identifier, literal("]]"))
  fixed annotation_aliased     = seq(literal("[["), identifier, literal("|"),
                                     until_close_annotation, literal("]]"))
  fixed annotation             = variant(annotation_bare, annotation_aliased)

  # ===== code-span `` `code` `` =====
  # Backtick-delimited semantic hook (NOT just monospace styling).
  # Corpus witness: Piece-Agents :24 "`END LOOP`", :30 "`JUMP LOOP`",
  # :50 "`LOOP:`". The corpus uses code-spans as first-class semantic
  # gestures (system-verbs, invocations, framings).
  fixed code_span              = seq(literal("`"), until_backtick, literal("`"))

  # ===== corpus-link `[text](wiki:Piece - X)` =====
  # Cross-piece reference at corpus altitude. Corpus witness:
  # Piece-Consciousness :86 "[distributed system](wiki:Piece -
  # Distributed Systems)"; Piece-Agents :81
  # "[Who pays the cost?](wiki:Piece - Agents)"; Piece-Fragmentation
  # multiple.
  fixed corpus_link            = seq(literal("["), until_close_bracket, literal("]"),
                                     literal("(wiki:"), until_close_paren, literal(")"))

  # ===== external-link `[text](URL)` =====
  # Standard markdown-shape external reference. Corpus witness:
  # universal (every published piece).
  fixed external_link          = seq(literal("["), until_close_bracket, literal("]"),
                                     literal("("), until_close_paren, literal(")"))

  # ===== inline image `![alt](URL)` =====
  # Corpus witness: Piece-Fragmentation §3
  # "![Developmental (In)variant](wiki:Developmental (In)variant)".
  fixed inline_image           = seq(literal("!["), until_close_bracket, literal("]"),
                                     literal("("), until_close_paren, literal(")"))

  # ===== density marker `TL;DR: <string>` =====
  # Per-section density collapse marker. Alex places TL;DRs at
  # section-ends (universal in Piece-Agents, Piece-Fragmentation,
  # Piece-Distributed) and occasionally with soft-break marker
  # `TL;DR:\\` (Piece-Consciousness §"TCP Over UDP").
  fixed density_marker         = seq(literal("TL;DR:"), whitespace_no_newline, line, newline)
  fixed density_marker_soft    = seq(literal("TL;DR:\\"), newline, line, newline)

  # ===== emphasis marks =====
  # Corpus witness: `**bold**` universal (Piece-Consciousness §Sources
  # table); `*emphasis*` less frequent but attested.
  fixed strong                 = seq(literal("**"), until_double_star, literal("**"))
  fixed emphasis               = seq(literal("*"), until_single_star, literal("*"))

  # ===== emoji first-class =====
  # Emoji are load-bearing semantic carriers, not decoration. Corpus
  # signature: `🌱` (Reed), `🌈` (Alex), `📉` (metric-collapse per
  # Piece-Agents :25 "Regulation goes 📉"). Per Reed 2026-08-03 charter:
  # "Emoji as first-class carrier."
  fixed emoji                  = charset(emoji_scalar)

  # ===== soft-break `\\\n` =====
  # Line continuation marker. Corpus witness: Piece-Fragmentation §1
  # opening lines every line ends with `\` for line-continuation without
  # paragraph-break. Preserves the vertical rhythm.
  fixed soft_break             = seq(literal("\\"), newline)

  # ===== quote-block `> line` =====
  # Multi-line quote per markdown convention. Corpus witness:
  # universal (Piece-Consciousness §Setup for Descartes quote;
  # Piece-Distributed §Message-passing for [[Actor]] definition).
  fixed quote_line             = seq(literal(">"), whitespace_no_newline, line, newline)
  fixed quote_block            = repeat(quote_line, 1, none)

  # ===== separator `---` between sections =====
  # Horizontal-rule/section-break marker. Distinct from frontmatter
  # (which uses matched `---` fences). Corpus witness:
  # Piece-Consciousness (multiple; between preview and members section).
  fixed separator              = seq(literal("---"), newline)

  # ===== list-item `- item` / `1. item` =====
  # Corpus witness: Piece-Fragmentation §4 (ordered practice list);
  # Piece-Distributed §Structure (unordered question list).
  fixed unordered_item         = seq(literal("- "), line, newline)
  fixed ordered_item           = seq(repeat(charset(digit), 1, none), literal(". "), line, newline)

  # ===== table `| col |` =====
  # Corpus witness: Piece-Consciousness §Sources table (Claim | Source).
  fixed table_cell             = seq(literal("|"), until_pipe_or_newline)
  fixed table_row              = seq(repeat(table_cell, 1, none), literal("|"), newline)

  # ===== section-cluster (structural pattern) =====
  # Alex's characteristic pattern-heading discipline: "When Agents
  # Enter the Room" / "When Agents Make Decisions" / "When Agents
  # Have No Body" / "When Agents Delete" / "When Agents `END`"
  # (Piece-Agents). The cluster IS load-bearing structure at the
  # composition altitude — a first-class semantic beat pattern. The
  # grammar admits arbitrary heading text; the CLUSTER discipline
  # is enforced at the @gestalt graph altitude, not at the file
  # grammar altitude.

  # ===== line-break-as-structure (architectural invariant) =====
  # Each `\n` is a semantic break, NOT prose-flow. The .gestalt
  # register does NOT permit reflow. Renderers targeting HTML/PDF
  # MUST preserve line-breaks; renderers targeting flowing prose
  # incur measurable L(ϕ) loss per @gestalt.render bilateral.
}

# === render — .gestalt AST → text via Wadler/Bernardy doc combinators ===
#
# Per @facet/mirror.render precedent (shards/code/mirror.mirror lines
# 219-282): render IS the language-altitude projection (AST → text)
# using Wadler 2003 + Bernardy 2017 pretty-printer combinator algebra.
# For @facet/gestalt specifically, the round-trip discipline is
# LOAD-BEARING:
#
#   parse(render(doc)) = doc  structurally
#
# Because the .gestalt corpus is authoritative (Alex's authored bytes),
# the render body MUST preserve every register-honoring pattern
# extracted above — asymmetric brackets, breath-marks, emoji, soft
# breaks, corpus-links. Sanitization = loss = broken round-trip.
#
# Body `\` per consumer-pull; the FLOOR resolver at cascade altitude
# discharges the concrete Wadler doc algebra binding.
render(ast) -> text { \ }

# === Round-trip identity — the register-preservation contract ===
#
# Per @facet/mirror precedent + Reed 2026-08-03 charter register-
# honoring discipline: for every valid .gestalt AST, the render →
# parse cycle IS the identity. This law IS what makes the .gestalt
# corpus a stable substrate value (each of the 19 published pieces
# is content-addressed; any lossy renderer would break the identity
# and desynchronize corpus from graph).
#
# Declared here as substrate property; the FLOOR resolver at cascade
# altitude discharges when render body lands.
requires round_trip(render)

out @facet/gestalt
out @facet/gestalt/grammar
